WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:18.140
A zero-population zone, with zero residents all year long.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:27.880
Suddenly, it becomes home to 2 million people from over 100 nationalities.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:32.840
And suddenly, the population returns to zero in just 12 hours.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.740
We are here in Arafat, al-rahma Mount, and Hajj.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:52.050
Before we begin, let’s go back in time and look at the number of pilgrims throughout history.

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:56.490
We’ll find that the numbers did not exceed tens of thousands each year.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:01:00.290
So, things were easy, and managing them was simple.

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:06.850
To the extent that Al-Madina Newspaper announced in 1964 the biggest Hajj in the Kingdom’s history — imagine that.

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:09.430
How many people do you think there were?

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.530
Only 128,000 pilgrims.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:17.830
After that, with easier travel and technology, the numbers increased year after year.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:23.630
The first year the number of pilgrims reached one million was in 1979.

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:29.250
And just 16 years later, the number of pilgrims reached 2 million.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:33.850
That’s forty times the number of people who used to perform Hajj in the past.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:45.800
Today, Arafat, 7 AM.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:49.000
The pilgrims started arriving at Arafat from Mina.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:53.600
How is this massive crowd managed from here?

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.200
The Command and Control Center.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.840
Welcome, doctor. May God give you strength.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:59.380
What are the biggest challenges in Mina?

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:01.820
The challenge in Mina is that it has specific religious boundaries.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.320
So it’s a limited space.

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:03.680
Confined.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:04.420
You can't expand it.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:05.440
.................................................

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:07.440
You have to accommodate 2 million within 24 hours.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:07.780
Suddenly.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:09.840
Just to give you an idea about the density...

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:12.020
The most densely populated cities in the world...

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:13.380
Manila in the Philippines...

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:17.580
Has around 40,000 people per square kilometer.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.000
Okay, let’s take another place...

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.880
With even more crowds than cities...

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.480
Like Disneyland, for example...

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:28.360
Its population density is 116,000 people per square kilometer.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:29.400
Mina...

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.720
We’re talking about 1 million people per square kilometer.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:38.220
That’s ten times the density of Disneyland.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:41.860
And maybe 15 to 20 times the most crowded cities in the world.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.640
This density leads to challenges...

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.380
Challenges in their movement...

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:48.240
Challenges in healthcare...

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.540
Challenges in the services provided...

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:52.540
Water, toilets, accommodation...

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:56.560
Major challenges arising from the extreme density.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:59.160
We create service-oriented cities...

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.900
And move cities three or four times a day.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:02.940
From Arafat to Mina...

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:05.260
2 million people moved on the Day of Tarwiyah...

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:06.200
Within the same city...

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.020
With the same facilities...

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.020
With the same services...

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.580
To Arafat, from Arafat to Muzdalifah...

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.260
Muzdalifah to Mina, and from here to the Haram.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:14.080
We move a city every 6 to 7 hours.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:18.420
Here we’re talking about more than 100 nationalities coming from every distant path.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:19.120
I’m from Jordan.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:19.920
From Zarqa.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.960
Welcome, people of Zarqa.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:21.880
Welcome people of Egypt.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:22.360
India.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:23.820
Pakistan.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.400
India, India, Pakistan.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.080
Kurdistan.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:26.640
Mashallah.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:27.740
Welcome, happy Yemen.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:31.360
In Arafat, it’s said that one of the reasons behind the name “Arafat”...

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:32.180
...is the idea of knowing one another.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:33.500
The concept of “so that you may know one another.”

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.460
Because people from all over the world come here.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:37.440
Different cultures.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:38.800
Different social classes.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:40.120
What does "know one another" mean?

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.880
When someone tells you to get to know a person...

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:42.780
What does that mean?

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.160
It means to understand their values.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.260
Understand their thoughts.

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:46.040
Their traditions.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:46.580
Their food.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:47.360
Their customs.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.440
All of that falls under the concept of knowing one another.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:52.540
And the more we know each other, the more we can coexist.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:53.340
Where are you from?

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:53.860
Nigeria.

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:54.960
Nigeria?

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:55.700
Lagos?

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:56.440
Karu.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:57.720
Karu? Mashallah.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:58.400
Nigeria?

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.920
My father used to work in Nigeria.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:01.700
At the Saudi embassy.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:04.320
My sister was born in Lagos.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:05.460
Mashallah.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:07.720
In 1961.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.780
Teach me a Moroccan word I don’t know.

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:10.360
Tanjia.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:11.460
Tanjia?

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:12.180
Tanjia.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:13.680
What is that — a dish?

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:14.480
A Moroccan dish.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:14.920
Tanjia.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:16.519
Specifically from Marrakesh.

00:04:16.519 --> 00:04:17.940
Do you have to say it like that?

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:18.660
Tanjia.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:19.339
Tanjia.

00:04:19.339 --> 00:04:21.029
Marrakesh-style Tanjia.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.820
Alright, we’ll come to Marrakesh and you’ll host us with Tanjia.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.540
Tell me — what impressed you the most?

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:25.960
The organization.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:27.780
The organization.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.480
That’s the most important thing for you?

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:31.820
How many cameras are we talking about?

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:32.940
More than 8,000 cameras.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:33.860
Just in the holy sites?

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:34.420
Just in the holy sites.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:36.780
We’ll see them later when we talk about the buses.

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:37.740
This, of course...

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:38.480
This...

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.620
22,244 buses.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:43.580
They give you the exact number.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:46.920
Each bus — what it is, how fast it is, everything.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:47.520
Every bus.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.200
Every bus.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.060
To the point where they know if each bus is stationary or moving.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:52.640
If it’s moving, what its speed is.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.420
And all of it is connected to AI.

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:55.360
Yes, that’s right.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:56.620
The 20,000 buses...

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.200
All are being monitored.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.000
I’m getting dizzy.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.260
What’s the challenge you face on the Day of Arafat?

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.380
The challenge in Arafat...

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:05.220
Is that this entire gathering of 2 million...

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:07.560
...must move within a limited timeframe of 5 hours...

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:09.420
...to Muzdalifah.

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:10.960
Do all of them have to go by bus?

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.640
They go up to Muzdalifah.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.600
These train stations move 320,000.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:18.120
Traditional transport moves 800,000 pilgrims.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:20.960
And this shuttle transport moves 750,000 pilgrims.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:22.600
What do you mean by shuttle transport?

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:23.700
Shuttle bus transport.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:24.640
Shuttle bus.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.660
That makes multiple trips.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:28.080
Exactly — back and forth.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:28.860
Back and forth.

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:30.380
We have one walking path...

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:31.120
For those who prefer to walk.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:31.960
For those who prefer to walk.

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:34.020
There are between 100,000 to 150,000 pilgrims

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:34.960
Who wish to walk.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:37.880
They also have designated areas in Muzdalifah to settle.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:39.480
Away from the transport routes.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:40.640
Ah, so they don’t mix.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:43.320
The issue used to be that the transport route was the pedestrian route.

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:44.380
They walked on the same street.

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:45.280
I remember back in the day.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.040
But that has changed, praise be to God.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:50.380
One of the evacuation paths from Arafat to Muzdalifah

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:52.020
Is the pedestrian path.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:54.240
Back then, speaking of walking...

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:55.960
They used to walk in the same area as the buses.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:56.980
Total chaos.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:05:58.300
And of course, it was dangerous for pilgrims.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:01.300
Today the paths are dedicated only for pedestrians.

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:03.380
150,000 walking pilgrims.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.500
Perform the evacuation.

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:08.340
From Arafat to Muzdalifah.

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:23.190
Welcome, welcome.

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:24.970
One of the provided healthcare services...

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:28.310
Is the convoy of hospitalized patients.

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:29.550
They had health issues during Hajj.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:31.450
They had emergency cases.

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:32.970
And were admitted to hospitals.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:34.490
So that they don't miss Hajj...

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:35.850
They are brought in this convoy.

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:37.530
So that they can be in Arafat.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:38.690
Because Hajj is Arafat.

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:39.890
A very beautiful scene, honestly.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.260
Welcome, welcome.

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:49.500
May God give you strength, brother.

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:52.080
Do you know the condition you have here?

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:54.400
She has a fractured hand and diabetes.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:55.300
A woman, right?

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:57.980
And this convoy came from Medina.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.380
This is just one of several convoys.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.180
Some come from Jeddah.

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:03.820
From Taif and from Mecca.

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:05.420
My heart fluttered with joy.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:06.600
When I saw the convoy, honestly.

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:07.860
The way it looked coming in...

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:10.040
These people were limited by their health...

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:11.480
Due to not even a major issue.

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:12.660
Just that they were in the hospital.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:13.420
They still get to perform Hajj.

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:15.700
And can fulfill all the rituals.

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.140
So we said let’s bring them along.

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:19.260
There are 11 different nationalities.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:20.020
Where from?

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:21.520
From Guinea.

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:22.220
Here from Guinea.

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:22.960
From Morocco.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:23.620
Pakistan.

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:25.180
From India, from Bangladesh.

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:26.200
From Ivory Coast.

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:27.100
Nigeria.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:27.860
Pakistani.

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:29.140
From South Africa.

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:29.840
From Algeria.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:31.180
A case from Algeria.

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.180
Welcome back safely.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.260
God bless you.

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:34.060
What happened to you?

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:34.500
Dizziness.

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:36.300
Like a sudden breeze.

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:37.680
And I lost consciousness.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.080
So they admitted me to the hospital.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:39.780
In Medina.

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:41.340
So you didn’t know they’d bring you here?

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:42.300
You thought it was over?

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:42.820
They told me...

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:44.300
Just a day before.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:45.520
So you just found out yesterday?

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:45.840
Yes.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.880
I didn’t know what surprise was waiting for me.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:48.580
Best surprise ever.

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:50.320
Administrative rule:

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:51.580
If you cannot measure it...

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:52.560
...you cannot manage it.

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:53.740
If you can’t measure it...

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:55.020
...you can’t manage it.

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:56.920
So how do you manage the healthcare system...

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:58.240
...for two million pilgrims...

00:07:58.240 --> 00:07:59.040
...in five days?

00:07:59.040 --> 00:07:59.960
We are in the center...

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:02.220
...for crisis and disaster and emergency management.

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:02.580
And operations.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:04.660
I have this screen here.

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:05.780
This is intensive care.

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:06.440
Praise be to God.

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:07.260
The situation is comfortable.

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:09.060
All hospitals are in the green zone.

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:10.240
If there's pressure...

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:11.180
...it turns red immediately.

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:12.420
They know there's an emergency.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:13.380
They must address it.

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:14.300
I contact the Red Crescent.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:15.320
The Red Crescent is right next to us here.

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:18.760
Okay, so let's take an example here.

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.580
Let’s look at the intensive care unit.

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:22.360
What cases are there currently?

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:23.660
Right now, the time is...

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:24.400
...12:30 PM

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.000
On the Day of Arafah.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:27.500
Since this morning, we have...

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:29.700
...received 160 admission cases.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:30.240
Admissions.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:32.059
And the emergency has received over 200 cases.

00:08:32.059 --> 00:08:32.559
Also...

00:08:32.559 --> 00:08:33.780
We have 600 more cases...

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:34.980
...in outpatient clinics.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:36.200
All received this morning.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:37.360
So you're currently on alert?

00:08:38.419 --> 00:08:40.940
We’ve provided over 50,000 medical services so far.

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:41.820
This Hajj season.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:42.580
This Hajj season.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:43.680
And we’re not done yet.

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:44.780
We haven’t even fully started!

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:45.900
We haven't said Besmellah "We have a lot of work on"

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:46.880
Maybe last year...

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:47.900
...we reached around 200,000.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:50.780
I’m trying to absorb the numbers.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.700
You’re talking about 200,000 in one week.

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:52.800
Days.

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:54.880
From today’s convoy.

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:57.660
Do you know the case?

00:08:57.660 --> 00:08:58.480
Male or female?

00:08:58.480 --> 00:08:59.940
He had heart surgery.

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:01.760
He underwent open-heart surgery here.

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:02.660
At a heart surgery hospital.

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:03.680
Okay, you know him?

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:04.500
That’s another story.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:06.920
The number of open-heart surgeries and catheterizations...

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:07.620
...we’ve reached 800.

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:09.160
800 catheter procedures.

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:09.480
Catheter.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:12.180
And the number of open-heart surgeries exceeded 50.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:13.300
Thank God for your safety.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:14.060
Wishing you wellness.

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:15.800
Get well soon, God willing.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:17.920
You are the first pilgrim to enter Arafat this year.

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:18.880
Thank God.

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:19.820
I didn’t expect it.

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:21.340
I fear the usual would remain.

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:23.240
How long have you been planning to come for Hajj?

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:24.500
For 10 years.

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:26.900
These people, imagine...

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:27.680
They’ve saved their whole lives.

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:29.480
They’ve saved just for this day.

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:29.580
True. and then they come and suddenly have an emergency and can't come to Arafah 

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:34.580
Such a beautiful feeling...

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:35.400
What I see now...

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:36.160
They’re coming in...

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:37.000
They’re happy...

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:38.940
Want to meet the youngest pilgrim?

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:40.080
The youngest pilgrim.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:42.460
We were filming at Al-Rahma Hospital.

