00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:32.660
Yes.

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:33.180
Protection.

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:33.620
Yes.

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:34.420
Inner peace.

00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:34.640
Yes.

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:35.580
Health and wellness.

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:36.220
Yes.

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:37.120
And the highest level of Paradise.

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:39.000
Now you're asking for a lot! you're seek into greed

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:41.340
What did we say?

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:43.800
You’re generous and we deserve it, inshallah.

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:45.240
We’re monitoring a group of women...

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:46.060
With a set of symptoms.

00:17:46.060 --> 00:17:46.520
What do you mean?

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:47.160
Someone comes and says...

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:48.540
There’s a lot of foot trauma.

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:49.980
So we deployed stations...

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:51.320
For foot and ankle care.

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:52.300
These exist now?

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:53.360
Some are already in place.

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:54.080
But with mobile teams.

00:17:54.080 --> 00:17:55.900
Dedicated to foot and ankle care.

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:56.340
We’ll see.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:56.620
Inshallah.

00:17:56.620 --> 00:17:57.100
We’ll see.

00:17:57.670 --> 00:17:58.940
As Dr. Hani said...

00:17:58.940 --> 00:17:59.920
Foot injuries...

00:17:59.920 --> 00:18:02.080
This is the second case we’ve seen in five minutes.

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:03.080
Just in this area.

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:04.000
Wishing you well, sir.

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:04.720
How are you doing?

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:05.320
What happened to you?

00:18:05.320 --> 00:18:05.580
Walking.

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:06.580
Too much walking.

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:07.640
Wishing you a speedy recovery.

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:09.620
Walking on asphalt and sidewalks...

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:10.200
They're rough.

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:11.200
With long distances...

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:12.060
It causes foot injuries.

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:12.760
Therefore...

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:13.960
For the first time in Hajj...

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:16.320
We’re testing rubber flooring.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:19.300
It’s made from treated tires.

00:18:19.300 --> 00:18:19.700
Why?

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:21.600
To reduce pressure on the feet.

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:24.200
And thus lower the risk of injury.

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:25.980
We also used an insulating material.

00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:27.840
To reflect the heat...

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:29.080
Instead of absorbing it.

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:30.160
So we can treat...

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:32.280
Or at least reduce the heat levels.

00:18:32.280 --> 00:18:33.080
Here’s an experiment...

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:35.100
This shows me the temperature.

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:36.380
Here, I have the reading.

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:37.940
83.5

00:18:37.940 --> 00:18:39.020
Clear.

00:18:39.020 --> 00:18:39.140
Clear.

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:40.560
83.5 right here.

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:41.140
And here...

00:18:42.540 --> 00:18:43.900
71.8

00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:45.480
Alright?

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:47.080
I won’t take your time now, you’re in the middle of it.

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:48.080
But what you're doing...

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:50.000
I hope every viewer understands...

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:51.580
The efforts you’re putting in.

00:18:51.580 --> 00:18:52.160
Thank you so much.

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:53.920
May God reward you — in your scale of good deeds.

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:55.660
Every person you relieve of pain...

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:57.120
May a prayer come your way.

00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:58.820
And to us too with you, inshaAllah.

00:18:58.820 --> 00:18:59.160
Thank you.

00:18:59.160 --> 00:18:59.820
God bless you.

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:01.980
What’s this?

00:19:01.980 --> 00:19:02.640
Wow!

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:03.660
Thank you.

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:04.720
Ministry of Health.

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:05.980
May God bless you all.

00:19:05.980 --> 00:19:07.280
And expand your sustenance, my son.

00:19:07.280 --> 00:19:08.600
May righteous people support you.

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:08.900
Amen.

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:10.400
And protect you from illness.

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:10.960
Amen.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.400
The most important thing in life...

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:12.820
They say...

00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:14.640
The first wealth is health.

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:15.640
The first blessing...

00:19:16.660 --> 00:19:17.300
Is health.

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:18.980
If someone doesn’t have health...

00:19:18.980 --> 00:19:20.660
They won’t enjoy any other wealth.

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:23.920
Whether it’s money or other forms of health.

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:25.160
Alhamdullah

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:27.020
The simulation topic...

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:28.220
And the hypothetical scenarios...

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:29.640
Done before Hajj...

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:32.920
They run simulations for 12 different sectors.

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:33.780
Before Hajj.

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:34.680
The transport sector...

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:35.400
That’s one of them.

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:36.760
Many scenarios.

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:38.520
Health sector scenarios.

00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:40.160
Scenarios for sudden illnesses.

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:42.200
If a bus hits a crowd...

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:44.060
God forbid, for any reason.

00:19:48.110 --> 00:19:50.320
This is one of those scenarios.

00:19:55.760 --> 00:19:56.910
What’s the scenario?

00:19:56.910 --> 00:19:58.910
We’re assuming we’re in Muzdalifah...

00:19:58.910 --> 00:20:00.030
At 10 PM.

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:01.750
A bus veers off track...

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:02.890
For some reason...

00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:05.730
And runs over several people.

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:07.150
How would the response go?

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:07.890
What would happen?

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:09.170
They simulate this possibility...

00:20:09.170 --> 00:20:10.930
So that, God forbid...

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:12.630
If something like that happens, they’re ready.

00:20:19.970 --> 00:20:21.730
You’ll see in the same scenario...

00:20:21.730 --> 00:20:23.810
One person is being trained...

00:20:23.810 --> 00:20:25.430
He’s on-site...

00:20:25.430 --> 00:20:26.630
And there’s another one...

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:27.610
A controller.

00:20:27.610 --> 00:20:28.270
I ask him now...

00:20:28.270 --> 00:20:29.790
Is the patient responding?

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:30.650
The patient’s not responding.

00:20:30.650 --> 00:20:31.490
Oh, that’s serious.

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:33.610
What’s that coming out of you?

00:20:33.610 --> 00:20:35.170
Are you okay or not?

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:35.910
You look fine.

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:37.290
But seriously...

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:39.130
Each case is different.

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:40.690
Here there’s clearly a hand injury.

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:42.270
Like some shrapnel or something...

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:43.230
Here on his face.

00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:45.170
So it’s a detailed simulation...

00:20:45.170 --> 00:20:47.350
For how to deal with each specific case.

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:49.610
More than 6 or 7 agencies joined in...

00:20:49.610 --> 00:20:50.350
The Red Crescent...

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:51.270
Civil Defense...

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:52.770
Internal ambulance services...

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:53.650
Ministry of Health...

00:20:53.650 --> 00:20:55.330
There has to be coordination between them.

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:56.710
He told me this is just one...

00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:58.990
Of more than a thousand simulations...

00:20:58.990 --> 00:20:59.730
In Hajj.

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:01.990
They imagine all possible scenarios...

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:02.870
That could happen...

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:04.430
And prepare for them.

00:21:07.650 --> 00:21:08.610
The Jamarat.

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:10.730
Of course, the Jamarat is now a structure...

00:21:10.730 --> 00:21:11.330
A large facility.

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:12.430
Five floors.

00:21:12.430 --> 00:21:15.150
Crowds are managed in and out...

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:16.670
Based on specific systems.

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:18.510
For example, the ground floor...

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:22.010
And the first floor are for pilgrims coming from the east.

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:24.610
Second floor — pilgrims from the west.

00:21:24.610 --> 00:21:27.110
Third floor — pilgrims from the north.

00:21:27.110 --> 00:21:28.730
From four different entry points.

00:21:28.730 --> 00:21:31.230
Fifth floor — pilgrims from the south...

00:21:31.230 --> 00:21:32.610
Via the Mashair Train.

00:21:32.610 --> 00:21:34.110
And other routes.

00:21:34.110 --> 00:21:35.170
This ensures...

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:37.930
The movement flows harmoniously,

00:21:37.930 --> 00:21:39.830
smoothly and without pushing.

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:42.610
No congestion issues at all.

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:45.230
Every group moves according to

00:21:45.230 --> 00:21:46.070
a specific schedule.

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:49.490
There are more than 32,000 schedules,

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:52.970
each for groups heading to the Jamarat.

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:55.950
All this is monitored

00:21:55.950 --> 00:21:57.990
by artificial intelligence

00:21:57.990 --> 00:22:00.190
at the Command and Control Center.

00:22:00.190 --> 00:22:01.270
How many cameras did we say?

00:22:01.270 --> 00:22:02.650
308 cameras.

00:22:02.650 --> 00:22:03.810
Only for Jamarat?

00:22:03.810 --> 00:22:04.570
Yes, only for Jamarat.

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:07.310
The cameras Ms. Al-Anoud mentioned

00:22:07.310 --> 00:22:09.150
are monitored here.

00:22:09.150 --> 00:22:11.650
Every person who passes through

00:22:11.650 --> 00:22:12.950
is counted.

00:22:12.950 --> 00:22:13.870
On the first day,

00:22:13.870 --> 00:22:14.970
the day of Aqabah Jamarat,

00:22:14.970 --> 00:22:19.470
so far 1,258,591 pilgrims

00:22:19.470 --> 00:22:21.170
have completed the stoning.

00:22:21.170 --> 00:22:23.190
Currently, at this location,

00:22:23.190 --> 00:22:25.070
there are 30,000 pilgrims in the walkways.

00:22:25.070 --> 00:22:26.470
How are they distributed?

00:22:26.470 --> 00:22:26.730
Here,

00:22:26.730 --> 00:22:27.990
by floors,

00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:30.650
and according to congestion levels.

00:22:30.650 --> 00:22:32.350
I performed Hajj a long time ago,

00:22:32.350 --> 00:22:33.750
back in the good old days.

00:22:33.750 --> 00:22:35.790
Stoning at Jamarat was very difficult,

00:22:35.790 --> 00:22:38.010
because back then,

00:22:38.010 --> 00:22:38.890
we didn't have this organization.

00:22:38.890 --> 00:22:40.410
I remember those arriving,

00:22:40.410 --> 00:22:41.730
mixed with those entering,

00:22:41.730 --> 00:22:42.610
mixed with those leaving,

00:22:42.610 --> 00:22:43.650
causing chaos.

00:22:43.650 --> 00:22:44.530
No scheduling existed;

00:22:44.530 --> 00:22:45.790
everyone went whenever they wanted.

00:22:45.790 --> 00:22:47.530
It was extremely tough,

00:22:47.530 --> 00:22:48.670
and dangerous too.

00:22:48.670 --> 00:22:50.370
Now there's a radical change,

00:22:50.370 --> 00:22:51.890
in managing groups,

00:22:51.890 --> 00:22:52.770
structuring—

00:22:52.770 --> 00:22:53.530
What did we call it?

00:22:53.530 --> 00:22:54.750
Standard structuring,

00:22:54.750 --> 00:22:56.370
the standard pilgrim structure.

00:22:56.370 --> 00:22:57.630
How are they structured?

00:22:57.630 --> 00:22:59.670
How many pilgrims make a group,

00:22:59.670 --> 00:23:00.990
how many groups form a unit.

00:23:00.990 --> 00:23:01.470
We have a unit,

00:23:01.470 --> 00:23:02.370
which is the bus,

00:23:02.370 --> 00:23:03.550
47 pilgrims per bus,

00:23:03.550 --> 00:23:05.270
each bus has a guide.

00:23:05.270 --> 00:23:07.070
Four buses form one group,

00:23:07.070 --> 00:23:08.610
making a total per group

00:23:08.610 --> 00:23:09.730
of 188 pilgrims.

00:23:09.730 --> 00:23:10.890
Each group has a leader.

00:23:10.890 --> 00:23:13.650
Five groups form one larger unit,

00:23:13.650 --> 00:23:14.190
a group of

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:15.030
20 buses,

00:23:15.030 --> 00:23:16.750
940 pilgrims.

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:18.430
Each large group has its own leader.

00:23:18.430 --> 00:23:18.990
Come here,

00:23:18.990 --> 00:23:20.470
Regarding the grouping

00:23:20.470 --> 00:23:21.290
for Jamarat—

00:23:21.290 --> 00:23:21.970
as we said,

00:23:21.970 --> 00:23:22.830
it's all scheduled.

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:25.470
Every group has a leader,

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:26.470
and they walk together.

00:23:26.470 --> 00:23:27.030
To Jamarat.

00:23:27.740 --> 00:23:28.630
Let's go, which level?

00:23:28.630 --> 00:23:29.310
Which floor?

00:23:29.310 --> 00:23:29.690
Ground.

00:23:30.180 --> 00:23:30.550
Go ahead.

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:31.250
Look.

00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:32.850
They're going, and they know exactly where.

00:23:32.850 --> 00:23:33.770
I asked him, which floor?

00:23:33.770 --> 00:23:34.730
He said, the ground floor.

00:23:34.730 --> 00:23:35.870
This group is from Turkey.

00:23:35.870 --> 00:23:37.850
They’re coming based on their scheduled time.

00:23:37.850 --> 00:23:38.750
And this is just one...

00:23:38.750 --> 00:23:41.530
Of 32,000 scheduled entries for Jamarat.

00:23:41.530 --> 00:23:43.390
Just for Jamarat alone.

00:23:43.390 --> 00:23:44.430
Welcome, welcome.

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:45.110
Bless you all.

00:23:45.110 --> 00:23:45.830
Best of luck.

00:23:45.830 --> 00:23:47.770
And this brings us to a very important point.

00:23:47.770 --> 00:23:48.870
The Hajj permit issue.

00:23:48.870 --> 00:23:49.610
Some people...

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:50.850
Hopefully they're the exception,

00:23:50.850 --> 00:23:52.050
And not the majority...

00:23:52.050 --> 00:23:53.070
They don't understand...

00:23:53.070 --> 00:23:54.310
The importance of the Hajj permit.

00:23:54.310 --> 00:23:55.690
Why is the Hajj permit important?

00:23:55.690 --> 00:23:57.350
Because all of this crowd management...

00:23:57.350 --> 00:23:59.310
Is built on one thing: numbers.

00:23:59.310 --> 00:24:00.210
If the numbers change...

00:24:00.210 --> 00:24:01.730
The entire system falls apart.

00:24:01.730 --> 00:24:03.430
So if people enter without a permit...

00:24:03.430 --> 00:24:05.990
If the plan was built for 2 million pilgrims...

00:24:05.990 --> 00:24:07.790
And 3 million show up...

00:24:07.790 --> 00:24:10.330
It throws off the entire plan.

00:24:10.330 --> 00:24:12.090
And when the plan falls apart...

00:24:12.090 --> 00:24:13.450
What does it lead to?

00:24:13.450 --> 00:24:14.710
Congestion.

00:24:14.710 --> 00:24:15.490
Congestion leads to what?

00:24:15.490 --> 00:24:16.050
Injuries.

00:24:16.050 --> 00:24:17.730
And even deaths.

00:24:17.730 --> 00:24:19.150
It's a simple matter.

00:24:20.210 --> 00:24:21.670
The Hajj permit issue...

00:24:21.670 --> 00:24:22.090
It's not...

00:24:22.090 --> 00:24:23.430
A personal issue.

00:24:23.430 --> 00:24:24.210
Just a simple example:

00:24:24.210 --> 00:24:26.070
Let’s say people are going to a football match.

00:24:26.070 --> 00:24:27.750
A game, in a stadium.

00:24:27.750 --> 00:24:28.390
Imagine...

00:24:28.390 --> 00:24:29.130
People entering the stadium...

00:24:29.130 --> 00:24:31.490
Without tickets, just like that.

00:24:31.490 --> 00:24:32.970
There’ll be overcrowding.

00:24:32.970 --> 00:24:34.090
And you're talking about a stadium...

00:24:34.090 --> 00:24:35.430
With 50,000 people.

00:24:35.430 --> 00:24:37.090
We've seen examples...

00:24:37.090 --> 00:24:38.150
Where poor crowd management...

00:24:38.150 --> 00:24:41.070
In stadiums led to deaths.

00:24:41.070 --> 00:24:43.230
Because of mismanagement.

00:24:43.230 --> 00:24:44.870
And that’s just 50,000 people.

00:24:44.870 --> 00:24:47.310
Here we’re talking about 2 million human beings.

00:24:47.310 --> 00:24:49.430
That’s why we say:

00:24:49.430 --> 00:24:50.590
Do not come to Hajj without a permit.

00:24:50.590 --> 00:24:52.690
So that the services can be better.

00:24:52.690 --> 00:24:53.930
Awareness has increased, honestly.

00:24:53.930 --> 00:24:55.950
The awareness campaigns run by the Kingdom...

00:24:55.950 --> 00:24:57.910
And the various conferences...

00:24:57.910 --> 00:24:59.390
They’ve launched the "Makkah Route" initiative.

00:24:59.390 --> 00:25:01.310
Makkah Route finalizes the pilgrim’s process...

00:25:01.310 --> 00:25:04.230
From their home country before they even arrive.

00:25:04.230 --> 00:25:07.090
Let us show you a real case of the Makkah Route initiative.

00:25:07.090 --> 00:25:09.570
Of course, pilgrim services start from the passport control.

00:25:09.570 --> 00:25:11.910
One of the challenges is overcrowding...

00:25:11.910 --> 00:25:12.990
That happens in airports.

00:25:12.990 --> 00:25:14.850
Imagine — 1.5 million pilgrims...

00:25:14.850 --> 00:25:16.290
Arriving by air.

00:25:16.290 --> 00:25:18.750
Within a very short timeframe.

00:25:18.750 --> 00:25:20.630
More than 8,000 flights...

00:25:20.630 --> 00:25:21.810
Just to give you scale.

00:25:21.810 --> 00:25:24.930
Heathrow Airport receives 160 flights per day.

00:25:24.930 --> 00:25:27.230
We're talking about 8,000 flights...

00:25:27.230 --> 00:25:29.110
Arriving in a very short period of time.

00:25:29.110 --> 00:25:30.650
Naturally, this causes congestion.

00:25:30.650 --> 00:25:32.530
So they end up spending hours

00:25:32.530 --> 00:25:34.390
Just to complete passport procedures.

00:25:34.390 --> 00:25:36.510
That's why, as part of continuous improvement,

00:25:36.510 --> 00:25:38.810
The "Makkah Route" initiative was launched.

00:25:38.810 --> 00:25:40.630
Its goal is to speed up this service.

00:25:41.580 --> 00:25:43.690
Let’s take Mr. Abdulwahid and Mrs. Souad from Morocco,

00:25:43.690 --> 00:25:45.530
As an example.

00:25:45.530 --> 00:25:46.230
When they came for Hajj this year,

00:25:46.230 --> 00:25:47.990
They completed passport procedures

00:25:47.990 --> 00:25:49.630
While still in Morocco.

00:25:49.630 --> 00:25:50.750
What you’re seeing now in the footage

00:25:50.750 --> 00:25:52.670
Is at the temporary Saudi passport office

00:25:52.670 --> 00:25:55.090
In Casablanca.

00:25:55.090 --> 00:25:56.090
They stamped their passports and finished everything

00:25:56.090 --> 00:25:58.570
Without any crowds.

00:25:58.570 --> 00:25:59.650
When they arrived in Jeddah,

00:25:59.650 --> 00:26:00.690
They didn’t have to wait at all.

00:26:00.690 --> 00:26:01.690
No standing in lines,

00:26:01.690 --> 00:26:02.850
No passport queues or crowding.

00:26:02.850 --> 00:26:04.510
They went from the airport straight to the hotel.

00:26:04.510 --> 00:26:06.810
And their luggage arrived directly at the hotel.

00:26:06.810 --> 00:26:09.010
This initiative benefited one million pilgrims

00:26:09.010 --> 00:26:10.130
From seven countries.

00:26:10.130 --> 00:26:10.990
Their airport procedures

00:26:10.990 --> 00:26:13.670
Were expedited by 95%.

00:26:13.670 --> 00:26:14.830
God willing, this initiative will expand

00:26:14.830 --> 00:26:16.830
And spread everywhere

00:26:16.830 --> 00:26:18.650
So that all pilgrims benefit from it.

00:26:20.300 --> 00:26:33.360
Welcome.

00:26:33.360 --> 00:26:35.100
Mina on the Day of Tarwiyah.

00:26:35.100 --> 00:26:37.280
There are several narratives about the name’s origin.

00:26:37.280 --> 00:26:40.280
One is that water in Makkah was very scarce.

00:26:40.280 --> 00:26:42.540
So people would gather water to take to Arafat.

00:26:42.540 --> 00:26:44.020
To Mina and the holy sites.

00:26:44.020 --> 00:26:46.300
And that’s where the name “Tarwiyah” came from.

00:26:46.300 --> 00:26:47.940
Today, we have coolers.

00:26:47.940 --> 00:26:49.540
And they have their own stories.

00:26:49.540 --> 00:26:51.700
The topic of water and services...

00:26:51.700 --> 00:26:53.800
Is a whole subject by itself.

00:26:53.800 --> 00:26:56.920
Imagine the amount of water provided to pilgrims.

00:26:56.920 --> 00:26:59.940
We’re talking about one million cubic meters of water...

00:26:59.940 --> 00:27:02.420
Delivered to pilgrims daily.

00:27:02.420 --> 00:27:03.600
Just to visualize it:

00:27:03.600 --> 00:27:06.080
If we take the Empire State Building,

00:27:06.080 --> 00:27:08.680
One of the tallest buildings in the world,

00:27:08.680 --> 00:27:11.000
And filled it completely with water—

00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:12.060
From top to bottom—

00:27:12.440 --> 00:27:16.220
That’s how much water is distributed every day.

00:27:16.220 --> 00:27:18.620
Huge volumes of water...

00:27:18.620 --> 00:27:20.540
To serve 2 million pilgrims.

00:27:20.540 --> 00:27:22.140
As part of the tools...

00:27:22.140 --> 00:27:25.620
For continuous improvement — the Hajj Conference.

00:27:25.620 --> 00:27:28.340
Held over 50,000 square meters.

00:27:28.340 --> 00:27:30.680
This is the fourth edition, started in 2021.

00:27:30.680 --> 00:27:32.940
It’s an annual Hajj conference.

00:27:32.940 --> 00:27:35.400
More than 95 countries participate.

00:27:35.400 --> 00:27:37.220
150,000 visitors.

00:27:37.220 --> 00:27:40.020
All gathered for continuous improvement.

00:27:40.020 --> 00:27:41.300
Of the Hajj experience.

00:27:41.300 --> 00:27:43.560
The improvement starts now.

00:27:43.560 --> 00:27:45.820
They analyze and evaluate it.

00:27:45.820 --> 00:27:47.420
And next year, they implement systems...

00:27:47.420 --> 00:27:49.940
To enhance performance and reduce crowding.

00:27:50.820 --> 00:27:53.220
We have a meeting with the Minister of Hajj soon.

00:27:53.220 --> 00:27:54.140
And we’re preparing for next year...
